==============================================================================
S3. Legendre / Fatou-Grace placement of small power gaps (exact integers)
==============================================================================
For each L <= 400 take every K with |2^K - 3^L| < 3^L / L (at most one K for
L >= 6) and classify the reduced fraction of K/L: convergent, intermediate
(with j and whether j is extreme), or neither.  Three tiers of the hypothesis:
  tier A: |Delta| <= 3^L/(4L)  -> PROVED to force a convergent (Legendre)
  tier B: |Delta| <= 3^L/(2L)  -> PROVED to force |alpha-K/L| < 1/L^2, hence
          convergent or extreme intermediate (Fatou-Grace, CITED)
  tier C: |Delta| <  3^L/L     -> the task's hypothesis; only |alpha-K/L| <
          2.9/L^2 follows, which is NOT enough for Fatou-Grace.
hits with L <= 60 (K/L, Delta, tierA, tierB, class):
    1/1   Delta=-1                     A=0 B=1  convergent n=0
    2/1   Delta=1                      A=0 B=1  convergent n=1
    3/2   Delta=-1                     A=1 B=1  convergent n=2
    5/3   Delta=5                      A=0 B=0  intermediate n=2 j=1/1 extreme
    6/4   Delta=-17                    A=0 B=0  convergent n=2 (x2)
    8/5   Delta=13                     A=0 B=1  convergent n=3
   11/7   Delta=-139                   A=0 B=1  intermediate n=3 j=1/1 extreme
   19/12  Delta=-7153                  A=1 B=1  convergent n=4
   27/17  Delta=5077565                A=0 B=0  intermediate n=4 j=1/2 extreme
   38/24  Delta=-7551629537            A=0 B=0  convergent n=4 (x2)
   46/29  Delta=1738366812781          A=0 B=0  intermediate n=4 j=2/2 extreme
   65/41  Delta=420491770248316829     A=0 B=1  convergent n=5
   84/53  Delta=-40432553845953101497907 A=1 B=1  convergent n=6
total tier-C hits for L <= 400: 19
tier-A hits: 3, all convergents (checked)
tier-B hits: 11, all convergents or extreme intermediates (checked)
