==============================================================================
S4. Eliahou bridge: cycle min-element N forces the clock onto a convergent
==============================================================================
For a signed odd cycle at b=+-1 with all |n_i| >= N:  Product(3n_i+b)=2^K Product n_i
gives 2^K/3^L = Product(1 + b/(3 n_i)), so |Delta|/3^L <= (1+1/(3N))^L - 1 (sign +)
or <= 1 - (1-1/(3N))^L (sign -).  Tier A follows once L^2 < roughly 3N/4.
known cycles: nodes, b, word, (K,L), Delta, B, q, N=min|n|, |Delta|/3^L, Eliahou bound, tierA, tierB, class
  (1,) b=1 w=[2] (K,L)=(2,1) Delta=1 B=1 q=1 N=1 rel=0.3333 bound=0.3333 A=0 B=1 convergent n=1
  (-1,) b=1 w=[1] (K,L)=(1,1) Delta=-1 B=1 q=1 N=1 rel=0.3333 bound=0.3333 A=0 B=1 convergent n=0
  (-5, -7) b=1 w=[1, 2] (K,L)=(3,2) Delta=-1 B=5 q=1 N=5 rel=0.1111 bound=0.1289 A=1 B=1 convergent n=2
  (-17, -25, -37, -55, -41, -61, -91) b=1 w=[1, 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 4] (K,L)=(11,7) Delta=-139 B=2363 q=1 N=17 rel=0.0636 bound=0.1294 A=0 B=1 intermediate n=3 j=1/1 extreme
  (1,) b=-1 w=[1] (K,L)=(1,1) Delta=-1 B=1 q=1 N=1 rel=0.3333 bound=0.3333 A=0 B=1 convergent n=0
  (5, 7) b=-1 w=[1, 2] (K,L)=(3,2) Delta=-1 B=5 q=1 N=5 rel=0.1111 bound=0.1289 A=1 B=1 convergent n=2
  (17, 25, 37, 55, 41, 61, 91) b=-1 w=[1, 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 4] (K,L)=(11,7) Delta=-139 B=2363 q=1 N=17 rel=0.0636 bound=0.1294 A=0 B=1 intermediate n=3 j=1/1 extreme
  (-1,) b=-1 w=[2] (K,L)=(2,1) Delta=1 B=1 q=1 N=1 rel=0.3333 bound=0.3333 A=0 B=1 convergent n=1
